  "id": "basic-need",
  "term": "basic need",
  "definition": "In this work-related psychology context, a basic need is a fundamental psychological need such as competence, autonomy, or relatedness. Satisfaction of these needs at work is linked with supportive job conditions, lower burnout, and more positive job attitudes.",
